Make the analysis panel resizable.\n- Require explicit consent for shortened session uploads.\n- Improve remote sync target selection and skip offline HTTP hosts.\n- Harden container builds with distributed Debian mirror selection and automatic failover.\n- Align serialized JSON with Go 1.27 JSON v2 semantics.\n\n- Keep previously synced sessions browsable when their source files disappear.\n- Keep reconciliation moving past deferred sources and report full-resync finalization progress.\n- Discover OpenCode channel databases and recover legacy project working directories.\n- Recover Antigravity working directories and effort metadata, and group sessions across Git worktrees.\n- Support current Kiro CLI and Qoder CN layouts while handling incomplete Gemini and unsupported Trae sessions safely.\n- Show Devin session information in Usage.\n- Correct Claude one-hour cache-write pricing and Posit Assistant cache-write accounting.\n- Preserve legacy PostgreSQL timestamps with offsets.\n- Restore Grok agent-minute reporting and non-interactive session classification.\n- Keep daemon readiness waiting active throughout startup progress.\n- Keep virtual session rows aligned after sorting and route arrow keys to the active pane.\n- Stabilize Usage project filters and prevent password-manager prompts in the project picker.","reactions":{"total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}
